  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Total federal contract obligations to Florida are $21.9B for FY2026 to date. Award activity in Florida includes 145,515 awards with an average award size of $151K. Obligations are down 32.4% year over year. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer in the state with $14.9B in obligations, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs with $2.5B and the General Services Administration with $1.5B. Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing leads industry spending at $4.4B, and Other Heavy and Civil Engineering Construction follows with $2.3B. LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION is the top vendor with $2.5B, with a second LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION entry at $2.2B and THALLE CONSTRUCTION CO INC at $1.9B. Historical obligations show a multi-year rise through FY25 and a partial-year drop in FY26: FY21 was $25.7B, FY22 was $26.6B, FY23 was $29B, FY24 was $31.3B, FY25 was $32.5B, and FY26 is $21.9B. All figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How did FY2026 obligations compare with prior years?",
        "body": "Fiscal year obligations peaked in FY25 at $32.5B and then moved to $21.9B in FY26 to date. Obligations rose from $25.7B in FY21 through $32.5B in FY25 before the FY26 partial-year drop. Obligations are down 32.4% year over year for the current fiscal-year-to-date comparison."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and industries concentrate federal spending in Florida?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense concentrates the largest share with $14.9B in obligations. The Department of Veterans Affairs and the General Services Administration follow with $2.5B and $1.5B respectively. Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing and Other Heavy and Civil Engineering Construction concentrate industry spending at $4.4B and $2.3B respectively."
      }
    ]
  },
